ains and as  concerns grow that vaccines alone may  not be the long-term answer  so interest is building in iva mektin  with its potential  to be both prevention and cure  so much so that researchers at oxford  university are conducting a trial of  their own  although we're hopeful that vaccines are  going to do what's promised  the data is not very reassuring that  they're actually going to achieve  everything that they're setting out to  achieve but uh if they don't  we'll have another tool as as a backup  and is one that we can deploy now  while waiting for the vaccines right  there there's huge portions of the world  which don't have anything available to  protect them or to treat them  after intense lobbying by healthcare  professionals slovakia this week became  the first eu country to approve the use  of ivamectin as a treatment  for covid19 wider use  may not be far behind jonah hull al  jazeera
 

